          "note": "diagnostic_tells: 'Hipped roof of equal pitch on all four sides with no front gable. One dominant cross-gable and the house is Tudor Revival, not French Eclectic.' Overrides the inherited tudor-revival cross-gable value, which is precisely the wrong-style tell."
        },
        {
          "id": "gable-on-hip",
          "status": "forbidden",
          "note": "A cross-gable dominant enough to read as a gable-on-hip crosses c01's 25 percent front-elevation-width cap and converts the house to Tudor Revival."
        },
        {
          "id": "cross-gable",
          "status": "forbidden",
          "note": "The inherited tudor-revival canonical value; forbidden here for the reason stated on 'hip'."
        }
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "front_gable_width_max_pct": {
          "value": 25,
          "unit": "percent",
          "kind": "measured",
          "source": "french-eclectic.c01"
        }
      },
      "status": "drafted",
      "rule": "A hipped roof at substantially the same pitch on all faces, ridge short relative to the plan; no front-facing gable may occupy more than 25 percent of the primary elevation width -- c01, a hard constraint.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "judgment": false
