        }
      },
      "rule": "No traditional precedent exists; the garage is authored as one more hip-roofed subordinate volume continuing the wall material and constant-pitch roof discipline (c01), its door turned away from the principal elevation. A cross-gable wing is forbidden outright -- it presumes a gabled massing vocabulary this style does not have.",
